From 358e320a890197e9d58ad05c657d4a031ab67ec7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Corrales <deathcamel58@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 12:53:07 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 13/13] ARM: dts: rockchip: az01: mark the gpio-restart line as
 a power hold

The AZ01 boards' gpio-restart drives PWR_OFF_DELAY (GPIO0_B1), which does
not reset the board: it holds the power supply on through the CRU reset
that follows, which would otherwise drop PWR_HOLD and power the board
off. Removing the node makes "reboot loader" power the board off.

Mark it "power-hold", so the restart handler stops warning on every
reboot about a reset it is not meant to perform.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [vendor board support]
